Locomotive door controller
==========================

Setup
-----
- Orient this programmable block with its Forward axis pointing toward the
  locomotive's normal forward direction and its Right axis toward the right
  side of the locomotive.

Run commands
------------
- forward
- backward
- open left
- open right
- open both
- close
- close left
- close right
- close both
- switch left
- switch right
- switch both

Left and right are relative to the selected direction of travel. Opening one
side closes the other. The script broadcasts its saved state once when it
starts, then sends one message for each valid command. Commands are broadcast
on the connected-constructs range; no train ID configuration is needed. Avoid
having multiple locomotives controlling the same connected construct at once.
Other locomotive scripts on the same connected construct listen to these
messages and synchronize their door-side state without changing their own
selected direction or rebroadcasting received commands. If a receiving
locomotive faces the opposite way, it swaps the received left/right state into
its own direction-relative state. Orient each programmable block toward its
locomotive's normal forward direction.
